--- !u!114 &1135235885
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1135235883}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<b>Bunny Hop Privacy Policy\r</b>\n\r\nLast Updated: August 13, 2026\n\r\nThis
    Privacy Policy explains how Bunny Hop (\"the Game\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\")
    handles information when you play our 2D endless runner game.\r\n\r\nWe respect
    your privacy and aim to collect and use only the information necessary to provide
    the Game's online leaderboard functionality.\r\n\r\nBy downloading or using Bunny
    Hop, you acknowledge the practices described in this Privacy Policy.\r\n\r\n1.
    Information We Collect\r\n\r\nBunny Hop allows players to submit their high scores
    to an online leaderboard. To provide this functionality, the Game may process
    the following information:\r\n\r\n<b>Player Name\r</b>\n\r\nWhen submitting a
    score to the online leaderboard, you may be asked to provide a player name.\r\n\r\nThe
    player name is used to identify your leaderboard entry and is displayed alongside
    your score to other players who view the leaderboard.\r\n\r\nPlease do not enter
    your real name, email address, telephone number, home address, or other sensitive
    or personally identifying information as your player name.\r\n\r\nWe do not require
    you to provide your real identity in order to use the leaderboard.\r\n\r\n<b>High
    Score</b>\r\n\r\nWhen you submit a score, your score is transmitted to our online
    leaderboard service so that it can be stored, ranked, and displayed on the Game's
    leaderboard.\r\n\r\nWe do not maintain a separate local copy of your online leaderboard
    score for this purpose.\r\n\r\nUnity Gaming Services Information\r\n\r\nBunny
    Hop uses <b>Unity Gaming Services</b>, including Unity Leaderboards and Unity
    Authentication, to provide online leaderboard functionality.\r\n\r\nUnity's services
    may process information required to operate these services, including a unique
    Unity Player ID and IP address. Unity's Leaderboards documentation states that
    these items are collected as part of the service's operation.\r\n\r\nThe Game
    does not use this information to personally identify you or to create a separate
    personal profile about you.\r\n\r\n2. How We Use Information\r\n\r\nInformation
    processed through Bunny Hop is used for the following purposes:\r\n\r\n- To submit
    and maintain leaderboard scores.\r\n- To associate a submitted score with a player's
    leaderboard identity.\r\n- To display leaderboard rankings and scores.\r\n- To
    provide the online leaderboard functionality.\r\n- To maintain and operate the
    Game's online services.\r\n- To address technical issues, security concerns,
    abuse, or service problems where necessary.\r\n\r\nWe do not use player names
    or leaderboard scores for advertising purposes.\r\n\r\nWe do not sell player
    names, leaderboard scores, or other personal information to third parties.\r\n\r\n3.
    Where Your Information Is Stored\r\n\r\nLeaderboard information is stored and
    processed through <b>Unity Gaming Services</b>, rather than being stored solely
    on your device.\r\n\r\nUnity provides the infrastructure used by Bunny Hop to
    authenticate players and operate the online leaderboard.\r\n\r\nUnity may process
    information in accordance with its own privacy practices and applicable data
    protection requirements.\r\n\r\nYou can review Unity's Privacy Policy here:\r\n\r\n[Add
    link here]\n\r\nUnity's documentation explains that developers using Leaderboards
    are responsible for accurately describing the service's data practices in their
    own privacy policy.\r\n\r\n4. Local Storage\r\n\r\nBunny Hop does <b>not intentionally
    store a local copy of your submitted player name or online leaderboard score</b>
    on your device for the purpose of maintaining the online leaderboard.\r\n\r\nThe
    online leaderboard is maintained through Unity Gaming Services.\r\n\r\nHowever,
    the Game and the operating system may use ordinary temporary files, cached data,
    or technical data necessary for the Game and its services to function. Such technical
    storage is separate from maintaining a local copy of your online leaderboard
    information.\r\n\r\n5. Third-Party Services\r\n\r\nBunny Hop uses third-party
    services provided by Unity Technologies to provide online functionality.\r\n\r\nUnity
    Gaming Services\r\n\r\nBunny Hop uses Unity Gaming Services, including:\r\n\r\n-
    Unity Authentication\r\n- Unity Leaderboards\r\n\r\nUnity Authentication provides
    the player identity infrastructure required by the Leaderboards service, while
    Unity Leaderboards stores and ranks submitted scores.\r\n\r\nUnity may process
    information such as a Unity Player ID and IP address as necessary to provide
    these services.\r\n\r\nUnity's handling of information is also subject to Unity's
    own privacy documentation and policies.\r\n\r\n6. Public Leaderboard Information\r\n\r\nIf
    you submit a score to the Bunny Hop leaderboard, the player name you provide
    and the associated score may be visible to other players.\r\n\r\nBecause leaderboard
    information may be publicly displayed, you should choose a player name that does
    not reveal information you would not want other players to see.\r\n\r\nWe strongly
    recommend using a nickname or pseudonym rather than your real name.\r\n\r\n7.
    Children's Privacy\r\n\r\nBunny Hop is not specifically directed toward children.\r\n\r\nBecause
    Bunny Hop uses Unity Gaming Services, certain Unity services have specific requirements
    regarding child users and parental consent. Unity states that its Leaderboards
    service is not intended for applications with child users unless the developer
    has obtained Verified Parental Consent where required under Unity's Terms of
    Service.\r\n\r\nIf you believe that a child has provided personal information
    through Bunny Hop in circumstances where such information should not have been
    collected, please contact us using the contact information provided below.\r\n\r\n8.
    Data Retention\r\n\r\nLeaderboard information may remain within the Unity Gaming
    Services infrastructure for as long as it is necessary to operate the leaderboard.\r\n\r\nUnity's
    current Leaderboards documentation states that personal data is retained by default
    indefinitely, unless the relevant leaderboard is reset or the applicable data
    is otherwise deleted.\r\n\r\nWe may reset, modify, or remove leaderboard data
    where appropriate, including when required for technical, operational, legal,
    or privacy reasons.\r\n\r\n9. Data Deletion and Privacy Requests\r\n\r\nIf you
    would like to request deletion of information associated with your Bunny Hop
    leaderboard entry or Unity Player ID, you may contact us using the contact details
    below.\r\n\r\nPlease provide enough information for us to identify the relevant
    leaderboard entry or player account without unnecessarily providing additional
    personal information.\r\n\r\nWhere applicable, we will process requests in accordance
    with applicable privacy laws.\r\n\r\nUnity provides functionality that allows
    developers to delete player data from its Leaderboards service and to delete
    Unity Authentication player accounts.\r\n\r\nPlease note that deleting leaderboard
    information may permanently remove your associated leaderboard score and ranking.\r\n\r\n10.
    Data Security\r\n\r\nWe take reasonable measures to protect information processed
    through Bunny Hop.\r\n\r\nOnline leaderboard information is transmitted to and
    processed by Unity Gaming Services rather than being maintained solely on your
    device.\r\n\r\nHowever, no method of transmission or electronic storage can be
    guaranteed to be completely secure.\r\n\r\n11. Your Privacy Rights\r\n\r\nDepending
    on where you live, you may have rights concerning your personal information,
    including rights to:\r\n\r\n- Request access to information associated with you.\r\n-
    Request correction of inaccurate information.\r\n- Request deletion of your information.\r\n-
    Object to or restrict certain processing.\r\n- Withdraw consent where processing
    is based on consent.\r\n- Lodge a complaint with an applicable data protection
    authority.\r\n\r\nThe availability and scope of these rights depends on the laws
    applicable to your location.\r\n\r\nTo exercise an applicable privacy right,
    please contact us using the details below.\r\n\r\n12. Changes to This Privacy
    Policy\r\n\r\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect
    changes to Bunny Hop, the services we use, applicable laws, or our data practices.\r\n\r\nWhen
    we make changes, we will update the \"Last Updated\" date at the top of this
    Privacy Policy.\r\n\r\nWe encourage you to periodically review this Privacy Policy.\r\n\r\n13.
    Additional Information\r\n\r\nBunny Hop uses Unity Gaming Services to provide
    its online leaderboard functionality. Unity's services may involve the processing
    of information outside the country in which you live.\r\n\r\nFor additional information
    regarding how Unity handles player and app-user information, please refer to
    Unity's Privacy Policy:\r\n\r\n[Add link here]\n\nBy using Bunny Hop, you acknowledge
    that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy."
